# MinIO buckets

## Gate

Use when the user asks to list or create buckets, inspect bucket tags /
versioning / lifecycle / replication, or read cluster admin / data-usage
info on a MinIO (or S3-compatible MinIO MCP) surface. Skip bare "S3" for
another object store. Always load `minio-safety` with this rule.

Never invent a bucket name. Resolve from MCP listing this turn or from a
name the user pasted.

## Prefer MCP (dual namespaces)

Live MinIO MCPs share the same tool surface. Pick **one** namespace per
turn from the ask — do not invent which cluster:

| User signal | Prefer namespace |
| --- | --- |
| swarm / fleet / primary object store | `user-mcp_minio_swarm` |
| backup / DR / secondary store | `user-mcp_minio_backup` |
| unnamed / ambiguous | ask once, or list on the only ready namespace |

Do not invent a side CLI or raw HTTP client while the chosen MCP works.

| Need | Tool | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| List buckets | `list_buckets` | start here for inventory |
| Create bucket | `create_bucket` | explicit create verb; `bucket_name` |
| Bucket tags (read) | `get_bucket_tags` | resolved `bucket_name` |
| Bucket tags (write) | `set_bucket_tags` | `tags` as JSON string |
| Versioning (read) | `get_bucket_versioning` | status / config |
| Versioning (write) | `set_bucket_versioning` | `enabled` bool — gated |
| Lifecycle | `get_bucket_lifecycle` | read-only on this MCP |
| Replication | `get_bucket_replication` | read-only on this MCP |
| Cluster admin | `get_admin_info` | no args |
| Data usage | `get_data_usage_info` | no args |

## Discover first

1. Prefer the exact bucket name the user named.
2. Else `list_buckets` on the chosen MCP; match by substring only when
   unique.
3. If several buckets match, list names and ask once — never pick a
   production bucket by guess.
4. Confirm which MCP (swarm vs backup) in the receipt when both could
   apply.

## Create bucket

1. Requires an explicit create / new-bucket verb this turn.
2. Call `create_bucket` with the exact `bucket_name` the user authorized.
3. Receipt: MCP namespace + bucket name. No access keys.

## Tags and versioning

1. Read with `get_bucket_tags` / `get_bucket_versioning` before changing.
2. `set_bucket_tags`: pass `tags` as a JSON string; summarize key names in
   the reply, not secret-looking values.
3. `set_bucket_versioning`: needs an explicit enable/disable verb; state
   prior status from `get_bucket_versioning` in the receipt.
4. Lifecycle / replication tools are **read** on the live MCP — do not
   invent write tools for them.

## Admin / usage

1. `get_admin_info` and `get_data_usage_info` for cluster-level summaries.
2. Report high-level counts / capacity shape — not credentials, tokens, or
   internal host dumps beyond what the ask needs.
3. Pair with `list_buckets` when the ask is "what is on the store?"

## Swarm vs backup inventory

When the user names both stores or asks "primary vs backup":

1. Run the same discover pass on each ready namespace separately.
2. Report bucket counts and notable names per namespace — do not merge lists
   without labeling which MCP they came from.
3. Prefer read-only passes; cross-store bucket create is two explicit verbs.

## Lifecycle / replication (read-only)

1. `get_bucket_lifecycle` and `get_bucket_replication` describe policy — no
   write tools on the live MCP map.
2. Summarize presence (configured vs empty) and rule counts — not full policy
   JSON dumps with secret ARNs unless the user asked for that bucket only.
3. Point gated deletes and object work to sibling rules — do not invent
   lifecycle PUT APIs.

## Report shape

- MCP namespace used (`user-mcp_minio_swarm` or `user-mcp_minio_backup`)
- Bucket name(s) + action (list / create / tags / versioning / usage)
- Short finding (counts, versioning on/off, tag keys)
- Explicit note that access keys were not shown

## Out of scope

- Object upload / download / copy / ask — see `minio-objects`
- Delete / public ACL / overwrite gates — see `minio-safety`
- Non-MinIO cloud object APIs without a ready MinIO MCP
- Site-specific bucket maps — resolve from MCP, never invent

